+# Independent paper execution (offline, no broker)
+
+`python3 -B scripts/execute/run_paper_trading.py --help`
+
+This entry point never imports `src.settings`, `.env`, QMT, IB, account configuration,
+legacy watchers, or real holdings. Importing `trading.paper` does not open a database
+or contact any service. It is **not** the legacy dry-run intent logger: fills change
+cash and share lots in an independent SQLite transaction.
+
+## Account / authorization / clock
+
+Every command requires an explicit `--database` and `--account-id`. Initialization
+additionally requires `--init-cash`, `--seed-source`, `--authorization-id` and an
+explicit `--fee-model`; there is no default balance, migration or holdings seed.
+Only the future execution owner may initialize the user-authorized production
+paper account (1000000 virtual CNY, empty holdings). This implementation task
+initialized **synthetic scratch fixtures only**.
+
+- `--fixture --now <timezone-aware ISO>`: only a database below
+  `/Users/chenyang/.hermes/cache/scratch/` is allowed. The clock is explicitly
+  synthetic; historical/future fixture dates are not evidence of real market fills.
+- Without `--fixture`, the clock is the actual system clock; `--now` is forbidden.
+  The database must be below scratch or exactly
+  `data/execution/paper_<identifier>.sqlite3`. No directory is implicitly created.
+  Fixture and system-clock accounts cannot be mixed or converted.
+- The account's last execution time cannot move backwards. An already initialized
+  account cannot be re-seeded. A missing ledger/account rejects as
+  `paper_uninitialized`; ordinary execution does not create one.
+- `zero_fee_assumption` explicitly means **gross rough simulation, not net return**.
+  Alternatively `flat_per_fill --buy-fee <CNY> --sell-fee <CNY>` charges the explicit
+  amount on each actual fill, including separate partial fills. No real commission,
+  transfer tax, stamp duty or broker minimum is invented. The model is immutable
+  for that account.
+
+## Execution command
+
+```text
+python3 -B scripts/execute/run_paper_trading.py execute
+  --database <explicit paper database> --account-id <id>
+  --authorization-id <user-paper-authorization>
+  --plan <local JSON> --quotes <local JSON> --calendar <local JSON>
+  --order <local JSON> --quote-max-age <explicit positive seconds>
+  [--fixture --now <ISO with timezone>]
+```
+
+`init` and `snapshot` use the same explicit account/database identity. `snapshot`
+returns persisted cash, fees, lots, total and sellable shares, fills and order
+states; it does not query real assets or invent portfolio market values.
+CLI exit `2` means rejected/error; exit `0` can mean pending/partial/filled, so the
+caller must read `status` and `fill_quantity`, not equate exit success to a fill.
+
+### JSON contracts
+
+Order keys are exactly:
+`order_id`, `symbol`, `side` (`buy`/`sell`), `quantity` (integer shares),
+`limit_price` (CNY, .01 tick), `rule_index` (zero-based index into the selected
+stock's `entry_rules` or `exit_rules`). Reusing an id with different intent rejects.
+Pending/partial orders are re-attempted explicitly with the **same intent/id** and
+current quote/plan; there is no autonomous background queue. Rejected and filled
+orders are terminal and replay with `event=paper_idempotent_replay`,
+`fill_quantity=0` and the original cumulative `filled_quantity`.
+
+Quotes JSON is `{"quotes": [<quote>, ...]}`. Each quote requires:
+
+| Field | Contract |
+|---|---|
+| `symbol` | canonical supported `600/601/603/605xxx.SH` or `000/001/002/003xxx.SZ` |
+| `source` | nonempty source identity, not fabricated last-price fallback |
+| `trade_date` | `YYYY-MM-DD` or exact `YYYYMMDD` |
+| `observed_at`, `received_at` | timezone-aware ISO; observed <= received <= now; observed age <= explicit maximum |
+| `bid_price`, `bid_size`, `ask_price`, `ask_size` | CNY and integer **shares**; no depth = null price and zero size |
+| `last_price`, `lower_limit`, `upper_limit` | explicit positive .01 tick prices; all prices inside valid limits |
+| `suspended`, `at_upper_limit`, `at_lower_limit` | explicit booleans; limit flags must agree with last |
+| `board`, `security_type`, `is_st` | exactly `main`, `common_stock`, false |
+| `quantity_unit`, `lot_size`, `tick_size` | exactly `shares`, 100, .01 |
+
+Calendar keys: `source`, `reliable=true`, `published_at`, `coverage_start`,
+`coverage_end`, sorted unique `trading_days`. The current date and a next trading
+date for a buy must be covered. The `reliable` flag is the caller's attestation,
+not independent network/source verification. Both current time and quote time
+must be in the supported continuous sessions 09:30 <= t < 11:30 or
+13:00 <= t < 14:57 (China UTC+08). Auction / closing auction / lunch / holiday
+execution is intentionally unsupported, not silently filled.
+
+Plan: `schema_version=1.0|watchlist_plan_v1`, correct `trade_date`, nonfuture
+`generated_at`, `mode=dry_run`, `autonomous_trading_enabled=false`; any supplied
+live-order authorization must remain false. `meta.paper_trading_authorized=true`
+and `meta.paper_authorization_id` must match the CLI and seeded account. Existing
+`requires_user_confirmation=true` for live trading does **not** require a separate
+confirmation for each user-authorized paper fill.
+
+For buys only, `status=ok` is insufficient: `production_ready=true` **and**
+`research_completion_passed=true` must be explicitly present at plan/meta level;
+any contradictory/unready/reassessment flag rejects. Supply the existing
+`research_summary.json` and R6 primary payloads using `--research-summary` and
+`--r6-research` (API keywords `research_summary`, `r6_research`), or embed their
+snapshots as `meta.research_summary` / `meta.r6_devil_advocate`. No implicit data
+file lookup occurs; the formal plan need not be changed to match a quote.
+
+Research proof requires matching dates and nonfuture, timezone-aware generation
+order R6 <= summary <= plan <= execution; summary `orchestrator_status=complete`,
+`contract_checks_passed=true`, empty `contract_failures`/`timeouts`, explicit usable
+fetch severity, all R1–R7 `units.status=complete`, each contract `status=passed`
+and `research_status=complete`, and nonempty artifact source pointers. R6 must be
+complete/nondegraded, have `candidates_evaluated>0`, all required upstream usable,
+and explicit hard-reject/counter-argument lists. Zero evaluated + empty rejection
+list is **not** a pass. These are caller-supplied offline source snapshots, not
+cryptographic authentication or independent verification of research content.
+Canonical content hashes and source pointers are persisted for audit.
+
+`no_trade` must be explicit false, genuine global/stock conditions and rejected
+pool entries veto buys. R6 root/meta `hard_rejects`, `hard_rejects_applied`, stock
+flags and raw R6 hard-severity arguments all apply; D1 reject IDs resolve through
+the supplied raw research. Unresolved hard-reject IDs fail closed. The symbol
+must be uniquely in `execution_pool` without a watch/candidate/exit-only identity.
+
+Within the SQLite write lock, **every evaluable new-buy attempt** invokes both
+shared pure functions `evaluate_stock_buy_eligibility` and
+`evaluate_plan_buy_gate`. RR is recomputed on this validated quote's actual ask
+and selected entry rule, not trusted from a cached `eligible` marker or cached
+buy price. Results go into saved order JSON and actual-fill evidence. Missing
+cache is fine if all actual RR evidence and other gates pass; missing/invalid
+prices, insufficient RR, external blocked/unknown qualifications, explicit human
+review, real global vetoes and unknown/zero budgets still reject. Only exact
+engine-owned stale RR conditions/derived reviews can be superseded by successful
+recomputation; original inputs and the formal plan remain unchanged.
+
+If a plan declares a file kill switch, the owner must supply explicit
+`risk_limits.kill_switch_active=false`; account hard-stop thresholds likewise
+require an explicit inactive owner snapshot. This module never reads legacy
+runtime/configuration files to infer those states.
+
+Supported price-only entries: `trend_pullback_buy`, `low_absorption_intraday`,
+`divergence_pullback`, and `t_add_pullback` (the latter also requires an existing
+paper holding). A numeric two-element `buy_zone` enforces **both** bounds; the
+real producer uses `trigger_price` as its lower anchor for some pullbacks, so a
+zone is not erroneously reduced to `ask<=lower`. Without a zone, pullback ask
+must be <= explicit target/trigger. `leader_breakout` requires last >= trigger
+and ask <= an explicit max acceptable ask, with any zone also enforced. Numeric
+`pullback_zone`, `confirm_price`/`reclaim_price` and max-ask guards are evaluated.
+Engine entries with explicitly null trigger (one-word/no-valid-entry production)
+remain unsupported. `execution_logic`, `derivation_reason`, `price_src`,
+`engine_formula` and ordinary descriptions are audit metadata, not signal proof.
+Full real Pydantic dumps' null/default metadata is supported. Active unverified
+auction/volume/board/first-seal/T-round predicates, nonzero premium guards and
+unknown rules reject explicitly rather than being silently ignored.
+
+Supported exits: `stop_loss_break`/`intraday_break_exit` (last <= trigger),
+`take_profit_hit`/`t_reduce_resistance` (last or bid >= trigger). No invented
+`exit_at_open`, sector-switch, high-watermark or stop-loss-percent semantics.
+`time_window` supports valid `HH:MM-HH:MM` only. Stock top-level stop/take alone
+never creates an exit rule.
+
+Each buy fill atomically saves the **full original stock and exit rules**,
+canonical plan hash and source timing/order identity, both in fill evidence and
+`exit_plans`. New buys require an explicit usable price-exit source. An existing
+paper holding can sell from that saved source even if absent from today's pools.
+A current explicitly legal exit plan may update the saved management source,
+even if its trigger is not yet hit; stale replacements or malformed sources
+reject. Missing today's membership never implies forced liquidation, and a
+missing saved/current source never invents an exit. Budget/no-new-buy/RR/research
+buy gates do not block a legal sell; paper authorization, quote/calendar, price
+predicate, T+1 and no-short rules still apply. `snapshot.managed_exit_plans`
+exposes retained source evidence. The new table is created only at explicit
+initialization; preexisting old-format ledgers are not silently migrated.
+
+Explicit budgets: stock `max_position_pct`, rule `position_pct`, and risk limits
+`target_total_position_pct`, `max_positions`, `max_buy_orders_per_day`,
+`max_orders_per_symbol_per_day`, `block_prefixes`; explicit meta/derivation total
+caps further tighten the budget. Existing held symbols require current valid bid
+quotes for valuation; missing values cannot be treated as zero. Quantity is
+clipped to available cash including fees, all budgets, remaining intent quantity,
+and remaining displayed counterparty depth. Only 100-share ordinary-main-board
+lots are supported (including sells); STAR/ChiNext/BSE/ST/odd lots are explicitly
+unsupported here without restricting research/watch lists.
+
+## Accounting and matching guarantees
+
+- Buy fills at ask, sell fills at bid, only when marketable against the explicit
+  limit. Last is only a trigger/validation input, never a substitute fill price.
+- Each buy creates a dated lot with `sellable_on` from the explicit trading
+  calendar. Same-day inventory cannot be sold. Sales consume eligible lots FIFO,
+  never real holdings and never a short position. No-trade/RR/R6 **buy** gates do
+  not block a lawful existing paper sell.
+- Orders/intents and fills are separate tables. States are `pending`, `rejected`,
+  `partial`, `filled`; a genuine simulated fill emits `paper_filled`, never
+  `submitted`. No ask at limit-up is pending with zero fill.
+- SQLite `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`, foreign keys, full synchronization and a single
+  transaction cover cash, fees, lots, fills, idempotency, order state and consumed
+  depth. Failures roll everything back. Concurrent duplicate ids fill once.
+- Quote liquidity identity is source + symbol + canonical observation time.
+  Changing received time/order id does not replenish it. Changing an already
+  consumed observation's payload rejects. Displayed depth is shared across
+  accounts within this database; separate databases are separate simulations.
+
+## Isolation regression
+
+```text
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1 \
+TMPDIR=/Users/chenyang/.hermes/cache/scratch \
+python3 -m pytest --noconftest -p no:cacheprovider \
+ tests/test_canghai_paper_execution_20261023.py \
+ tests/test_canghai_paper_parent_review_20261023.py \
+ --junitxml=/Users/chenyang/.hermes/cache/scratch/canghai_paper_parent_review_20261023/junit.xml -q
+```
+
+Tests block network, child processes and reads of production data/.env; all
+SQLite databases/JSON fixtures are scratch-only. The actual multi-process CLI
+rehearsal and read-back evidence are separately under the scratch report folder.
+Remaining production handoffs: trusted quote/calendar/research snapshots and
+provenance, explicit readiness/owner kill-switch snapshots, execution-owner
+account initialization / scheduling, and user-facing consumption of paper fills.
+No production account, watcher, cron, account mode, plan, configuration or sign-off
+is modified by this work.
